RF.put("questb:b31",{"8511":{"id":8511,"t":"The Alliance Needs Light Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 50.","obj":"Bring 10 Light Leather to Bonnie Stoneflayer at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n10 Light Leather Tattered Chest 18 % , Battered Chest 18 % , Armor Crate 0 % , Tattered Chest 0 % and 4 more","desc":"We Stoneflayers have a long history of being skinners, ‹class›. That's why the Alliance has asked my family to help out with the collection of light leather for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort. I'm here to see to it that the leather is tanned correctly for whatever they want to put it to use for. But we need your help.\nSince I have to be here doing that, I need you to go out and collect the skins, returning them to me here. What do you say, lad/lass, will you give it a go?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"‹class›, I do so hope that's the light leather you promised.","done":"I dare say the Alliance is going to be very happy with your skins here, ‹class›. I'll make sure that not a one goes to waste. Thank you, and make sure that you check back in with me once I've counted them up to see if we need more.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.3,"y":33.4,"n":"Bonnie Stoneflayer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8591":{"id":8591,"t":"The Horde Needs More Thick Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Thick Leather to Sergeant Umala at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n10 Thick Leather Razzashi Cobra 37.5 % in Zul'Gurub , Felsteel Chest 7.1 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 4.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 4.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Druid, as you can see I still need to gather up more thick leather. Once again I ask your help with this task, and promise that if you complete it, you will be recognized for your efforts.\nTime is of the essence! Return to me with the thick leather so that we can finish our preparations and go to war, hero!","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"You did it, ‹name›, I knew that you would! Once again, thank you on behalf of the entire Horde. Your efforts have been noted and are greatly appreciated. And if you find yourself with more thick leather that you'd like to donate, bring them to me here.\nLok'tar Ogar, ‹class›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.1,"y":72.8,"n":"Sergeant Umala","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"511":{"id":511,"t":"Encrypted Letter","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Encrypted Letter to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.\nCleverly Encrypted Letter\nProvided: Cleverly Encrypted Letter","desc":"One of the letters on this table is encrypted and inscrutable.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes, ‹name›? Do you have some business with me?","done":"What is this? Hold a moment... let me take a closer look.\n...\nHm, I have never before seen this form of encryption, but I must admit that my knowledge in that area is by no means complete.\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":58.3,"y":67.9,"n":"Syndicate Documents","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":47.9,"y":82.2,"n":"Syndicate Documents","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.6,"y":57.1,"n":"Loremaster Dibbs","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8271":{"id":8271,"t":"Hero of the Stormpike","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBloodseeker Ice Barbed Spear Wand of Biting Cold Cold Forged Hammer\nExperience: 650\n+10 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":40.7,"y":79.6,"n":"Prospector Stonehewer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"671":{"id":671,"t":"Foul Magics","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get 10 Bloodstone Amulets for Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\n10 Bloodstone Amulet Syndicate Mercenary 38 % , Syndicate Pathstalker 38 % , Syndicate Highwayman 28 %","desc":"I have felt a strangeness in the air... a feeling that simmers in my blood. I had my suspicions. I set off to find the source of my unease and discovered to the west, at Northfold Manor, the residual traces of demonic summoning. As I got close, my blood began to boil and the rage within me grew.\nOn the ground I spied an amulet of bloodstone, used to assist in demonic summoning. The one I found was depleted, however. I'll need another to examine, but I dare not return to the manor. Can you bring me some?","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Once-cursed blood still runs through my veins, ‹name›. If someone... something is summoning demons, it must be stopped.","done":"It will take some time for me to ascertain the true intentions of the Syndicate, but their obvious association with dark, demonic magic troubles me. I will tell you when I know more.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"991":{"id":991,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":19,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Teronis in Ashenvale.","desc":"‹name›, a longtime friend of mine is also aiding the Sentinels here in Ashenvale, but he has yet to return.\nHe had leads on finding an item that he thought could slow the furbolg attacks on our people--a rod created by a now-dead, evil wizard.\nBefore he left here, he mentioned seeking out a gem for the rod.\nHe mentioned the gem possibly being hidden at the shrine in Lake Falathim at the base of the mountain to the west. The gem was being held there before it was overrun.\nFind my friend, ‹name›, please.","rew":"Experience: 1,450\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Teronis' body lies broken atop the island. For some unknown reason, the murlocs have left it alone.\nThe deep slashes across his corpse obviously came from the weapons and claws of the murlocs.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":20.3,"y":42.3,"n":"Teronis' Corpse","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"2751":{"id":2751,"t":"Barbaric Battlements","lv":32,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring two Patterned Bronze Bracers, two Bronze Greatswords, and two Sharp Claws to Orokk Omosh in Orgrimmar.\n2 Patterned Bronze Bracers\n2 Bronze Greatsword\n2 Sharp Claw Chieftain Nek'rosh 50 % , Legion Hound 13.2 % , Pesterhide Snarler 11.6 % , Pesterhide Hyena 10 % and 4 more","desc":"Twenty generations of Omosh have held this hammer, ‹name›. A hundred thousand tons of metal we have molded. Tragically, it all ends at Orokk, failure of the Omosh: Without kin and incapable of producing offspring.\nI cannot let the secret recipes of Omosh die with me! Someone must continue the legacy, Omosh or not!\nProve to Orokk you are capable, ‹name›. Bring for Orokk the following: Two patterned bronze bracers, two bronze greatswords, and two sharp claws. Bring them for Orokk and we shall continue.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Barbaric Iron Breastplate\nExperience: 2,550","back":"Bronze, ‹name›! More bronze!!","done":"The bloodline will fade but perhaps the legend of Omosh will continue!\nYou have proven that you are a blacksmith, ‹name›. For the blacksmith the reward is the satisfaction of seeing their weapons and armors coated in the blood of their enemies!\nMay the breastplates you create for the generations ahead be drenched in the blood of your enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":79.2,"y":22.4,"n":"Orokk Omosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97951":{"id":97951,"t":"Camping 101 alchemy","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Carolai Anise in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your alchemy skill to 20","desc":"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.2,"n":"Carolai Anise","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96031":{"id":96031,"t":"Camping 101 leatherworking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Gretta Finespindle in Ironforge to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your leatherworking skill to 20","desc":"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, ‹class›. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","done":"There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nDun Morogh Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":39,"y":32.8,"n":"Gretta Finespindle","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94351":{"id":94351,"t":"Craftsmans writ frostsaber boots","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Frostsaber Boots\nFrostsaber Boots","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Frostsaber Boots, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Frostsaber Boots Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94351","cats":["crafting"]},"94271":{"id":94271,"t":"Craftsmans writ ornate mithril shoulders","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Ornate Mithril Shoulders\nOrnate Mithril Shoulders","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Ornate Mithril Shoulders, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Ornate Mithril Shoulders Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94271","cats":["crafting"]},"94911":{"id":94911,"t":"Child of nature","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Greetings, young ‹race›. I can see that you have much promise in the druidic arts. There is one who you may want to speak with in the city of Thunder Bluff by the name of Turak Runetotem. He will teach you how to reach the stronghold of the Cenarion Circle on Kalimdor, Moonglade.\nYou will be welcomed there, and the druids of the circle will impart their knowledge upon you.\nAs your people would say--go with the wind's blessing, young one. I wish you good fortune in your adventures.","done":"A high elf, speaking to me... in Thunder Bluff. Will wonders never cease?\nWell, shaper of wind, let me join our Earthen Ring brothers and sisters in welcoming you to Azeroth. My fellow druids of the Cenarion Circle have much wisdom to impart upon you, child of nature.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22.4,"n":"Muln Earthfury","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.4,"y":27.6,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"31":{"id":31,"t":"Aquatic Form","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Idol of Shifting Tides.","obj":"Return to Thunder Bluff and show Turak Runetotem the Pendant of the Sea Lion.\nPendant of the Sea Lion\nProvided: Pendant of the Sea Lion","desc":"You have completed the necessary lessons all young druids are taught before they can adopt an aquatic aspect. Go now back to your trainer, Turak Runetotem, in Thunder Bluff. Show him your pendant and prove to him you are ready to learn what he has to teach you. He will complete your training, allowing you to become one with the water.\nGoodbye, young druid. We shall speak again.","rew":"New in Forever: Idol of Shifting Tides.\nYou will receive:\nAquarius Belt Idol of Shifting Tides\nYou will learn: Aquatic Form\nExperience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Your return to Thunder Bluff is not without heralding, though I will need proof of your lessons learned in Moonglade before I will teach you your aquatic form.\nDo you have the Pendant of the Sea Lion?","done":"Very impressive, ‹name›. Your ancestors would be pleased with your progress! You're ready to learn your aquatic form, and it is my pleasure to teach it to you.\nAlso, in recognition of your achievement during the two trials, I give you this item. I hope you'll find it to be a welcome addition to your gear as a protector of nature and a keeper of the balance.\nMoonglade Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"831":{"id":831,"t":"The Admiral's Orders","lv":7,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Nazgrel in Thrall's chamber in Orgrimmar.\nAdmiral Proudmoore's Orders\nProvided: Admiral Proudmoore's Orders","desc":"Humans cannot be trusted. We fought alongside them with a weary heart, knowing they would betray us one day.\nAdmiral Proudmoore's death was not enough to stop his legacy of deceit. The human scum had his plans well laid out before he ever met his demise.\nHis reign won't even die with Benedict it seems. Who knows how long it will be before the next waves of Proudmoore's men land upon our shores.\nWe need to get these orders to Nazgrel in Orgrimmar immediately! He can be found in Thrall's chamber.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Can you not see that I am busy? This had better be pressing...","done":"Countless times I urged the Warchief not to trust the humans, but personal pride is not what is at stake here.\nYou have served the Horde honorably, young ‹class›.\nNow excuse me, I must counsel Thrall on these matters at once...\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.9,"y":43.5,"n":"Gar'Thok","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":32.3,"y":35.7,"n":"Nazgrel","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1391":{"id":1391,"t":"Nothing But The Truth","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Zraedus's Brew to Infiltrator Marksen in Stonard.\nZraedus's Brew\nProvided: Zraedus's Brew","desc":"We need to operate with a certain amount of discretion. After all, it's not like you're going to waltz in there and convince the fool to drink Faustin's concoction here, right?\nBut if there's one thing those humans cannot deny it's the booze. I'll take Faustin's serum and mix it into this ale. I guarantee the poor sap will show no reluctance when it comes to chug-a-lugging a brew.\nMake haste to Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows, ‹name›. And keep our little mission nice and quiet...","rew":"Experience: 2,550\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Please have mercy on me! I have information that goes beyond alliance boundaries. While I am no sympathizer of the Horde, there is political treachery going on that must be revealed!","done":"A drink for me? How kind. It's been days since they've allowed me to drink. Let me drink this down and then I'll tell you what I've learned....\nDuskwood Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":87.8,"y":35.6,"n":"Deathstalker Zraedus","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":44.3,"y":52.4,"n":"Infiltrator Marksen","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"111":{"id":111,"t":"Speak with Gramma","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Gramma Stonefield.","desc":"Please, ‹name›, talk with my Gramma. If anyone can find a way to bring me together with Maybell, she can.\nShe's inside our house east of here.","rew":"Experience: 140\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"While our families are feuding, Tommy Joe and Maybell don't have much of a future, but... maybe we can get them together for just a little while.\nHm, what can we do...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":29.8,"y":86,"n":"Tommy Joe Stonefield","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":34.9,"y":83.9,"n":"Gramma Stonefield","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"6031":{"id":6031,"t":"Runecloth","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 30 Runecloth to Meilosh in Timbermaw Hold.\n30 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","desc":"In Timbermaw, we are content. We do not like strangers. This is good for us, but it is bad for trade.\nNot long ago, a rare night elf friend came to Timbermaw and she wore a runecloth cloak. Runecloth is rare among us, but the cloak was so fine my people want me to make more runecloth clothing.\nWill you bring me runecloth? If you bring me enough, then I will give you something in trade.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShadowskin Spaulders Bricksteel Gauntlets\nExperience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"Do you have the runecloth? My people are eager for more items of runecloth!","done":"Ah, you brought the cloth. Such fine material it is!\nThank you, ‹name›. You are a true friend. Please accept this in exchange.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":65.7,"y":2.8,"n":"Meilosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4111":{"id":4111,"t":"Salve via Skinning","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Patch of Tainted Skin","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve","back":"A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!\nWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.","done":"This is exactly what I need. Here - take these plant salves and use them to reclaim Felwood from the corruption. We must persevere, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3791":{"id":3791,"t":"The Mystery of Morrowgrain","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Morrowgrain to Quintis Jonespyre in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n10 Morrowgrain\nProvided: Evergreen Pouch","desc":"Let me to be frank with you, ‹name›. I'm interested - nay, concerned with why the Arch Druid in Darnassus is using the name of the Cenarion Circle as well as the Circle's resources to procure vast amounts of morrowgrain. I'm a researcher - curses are my specialty. I've heard that morrowgrain, under the right conditions, exude qualities like other herbs used in primitive curses.\nI want to know more, and I ask for your help. Bring me ten morrowgrain, and I will be sure to take care of you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nQuintis' Research Gloves Bark Iron Pauldrons\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I'm looking for ten morrowgrain - that should be enough to at least get my research started. I'll no doubt burn through a lot of those going down wrong paths, but such is the nature of research.","done":"Gah, these morrowgrain make me feel... weird. What in the name of Elune is Staghelm up to with these things?\nAnyway, thank you again for your help. Here's a little something... you know, for the effort. My research on morrowgrain is going to take a while, and I no doubt am going to need more. While I'm at it, I suppose I could take the time to see if morrowgrain have some pertinent alchemical uses. Still, I feel uncomfortable even being around them.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":32.4,"y":43.8,"n":"Quintis Jonespyre","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"8911":{"id":8911,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Dreadmist Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nDreadmist Bracers Summoned Blackhand Dreadweaver 3.5 % , Blackhand Dreadweaver 3.4 % , Smolderthorn Seer 2 % , Firebrand Dreadweaver 1.8 % and 3 more","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"271":{"id":271,"t":"Vyrin's Revenge","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Ol' Sooty then show your handiwork to Daryl the Youngling at the Farstrider Lodge.\nOl' Sooty's Head Ol' Sooty","desc":"I don't suppose you'd be interested in a little payback for His Boldness? Daryl does have some skill, it pains me to say.\nA year ago, a large bear had been the target of the Farstrider Lodge, but none of the hunters had any luck with him. So, Daryl thought he'd try his hand against him. All he had to show for his effort was that ugly scar over his eye.\nKill the bear, and I'm sure even Daryl would be speechless for once.\nThe bear, Ol' Sooty, can be found around his lair in the hills over Thelsamar.","rew":"Experience: 775","back":"Ah, ‹name›! Back so soon? No doubt you've been at the hunt again? Don't worry if you've had some setbacks, in the long run it will make you better!\n... You couldn't get much worse, anyway...","done":"Er... what's this? A bear's head, by the looks at it.\n<He runs a finger along his scar unconsciously.>\nWell, that's quite an interesting kill you have yourself there. Couldn't be that bear from back then...\n<He trails off then starts to visibly shake.>\nOh, take that away take it away! Get that grisly thing out of here!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":81.7,"y":64.1,"n":"Vyrin Swiftwind","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":83.5,"y":65.5,"n":"Daryl the Youngling","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8671":{"id":8671,"t":"Ragetotem the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":36,"y":80.1,"n":"Elder Ragetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"93791":{"id":93791,"t":"Speak with belann","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Belann Windwood in Valanaar.","desc":"‹name›, it is clear your skill with magic is growing and I believe it is time for you to partake in one of the High Order's oldest traditions for young and aspiring mages. It is time for you to craft a spell focus of your own.\nSeek out Belann Windwood in Valanaar. He has been crafting staves and wands for the High Order for over a century, so you will be in good hands.","done":"Ah, you must be ‹name›? It is heartening to see young mages eager to learn our ways and history. Come, I will explain the next steps to crafting your spell focus.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":65.8,"y":80.4,"n":"Anathamaas Aetherwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":62.8,"y":77.4,"n":"Belann Windwood","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1951":{"id":1951,"t":"Rituals of Power","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the book Rituals of Power to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\nRituals of Power Rituals of Power in Scarlet Monastery","desc":"Hm... now that I think about it, I don't have my book! You see, I had some gambling debts and to pay them off I sold the last copy of Rituals of Power to a member of the clergy....\nA member of the Scarlet Brotherhood. He must have taken it to their library in the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades!\nIf you want that book, then you'll have to go to the monastery to find it. And sorry about all the trouble. I'm not myself these days...","rew":"Experience: 3,150","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. Did you find the book, Rituals of Power?","done":"That's it! It's just what I need to prepare for the ritual to create your wand! I hope it wasn't too much trouble to find...\nThousand Needles Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.3,"y":75.7,"n":"Magus Tirth","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"751":{"id":751,"t":"The Ravaged Caravan","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Venture Co. Documents to Morin Cloudstalker near Bloodhoof Village.\nVenture Co. Documents\nProvided: Venture Co. Documents","desc":"Prying open the lid reveals a tightly packed assortment of ore and minerals, more evidence of the Venture Co.'s mining operation in Mulgore. On the top of the ore and minerals you remove a tightly bound sheaf of papers.\nUp in the foothills to the east, you can barely hear the sounds of work, and see smoke rising from a large fire.","rew":"Experience: 525\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Hail, ‹name›. Have you learned anything new about the Venture Co.'s plans and operations in our homeland?\nIf they plan to exploit our lands as they have others, the Outrunners will be quick to put an end to it.","done":"It does indeed appear that the Venture Co. is attempting to rob us of our natural resources. It is good to know this for true, and now it seems, we must do something about it.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":51.9,"y":53.4,"n":"Sealed Supply Crate","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":54.8,"y":64.3,"n":"Morin Cloudstalker","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9071":{"id":9071,"t":"Earthshatter Spaulders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Earthshatter Spaulders if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Spaulders, 12 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 2 Arcanite Bars and 2 Mooncloth.\nDesecrated Spaulders Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcanite Bar\n2 Mooncloth","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Spaulders\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Earthshatter Spaulders.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"4511":{"id":4511,"t":"Calm Before the Storm","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Bank Voucher to Karus in the bank of Orgrimmar.\nBank Voucher\nProvided: Bank Voucher","desc":"‹name›, we could not have gotten this far without you. The time will come soon, no doubt, when I'll ask for your help against the silithid once more. We must absorb what we have learned in Un'Goro; I fear that my assumptions that the silithid originated from Un'Goro are now wrong... that indeed there is a far stronger presence somewhere.\nTake this note to Karus at the bank. He'll give you something from my vault that should be viewed as a token of my gratitude. Thank you for your assistance, mighty ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOblivion Orb Snarkshaw Spaulders Eschewal Greaves\nExperience: 8,150\n+200 reputation with Horde","back":"Zug zug! What may I help you with today, ‹class›?","done":"This bank voucher authorizes me to withdraw an item from Zilzibin Drumlore's account with us and present it to you. Congratulations would seem to be in order!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":56.3,"y":46.7,"n":"Zilzibin Drumlore","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.6,"y":69.1,"n":"Karus","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5631":{"id":5631,"t":"Returning Home","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"A priestess recently visited our halls seeking you out, young ‹race›. She said that she was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out a Priestess Alathea--she will tell you more.\nThe Light be with you, ‹name›.","rew":"You will learn: Starshards\nExperience: 210","done":"Wonderful, you've returned home, ‹name›. It always pleases Tyrande and myself when those we've trained go out into the world and return to us safely. How have things been with you? Does Elune still bless your travels? Perhaps after we speak more about the business at hand, you could tell me more of your travels.\nStormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":45.2,"n":"Brother Joshua","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8831":{"id":8831,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Stormwind. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.4,"y":74.5,"n":"Officer Maloof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"8351":{"id":8351,"t":"Bor Wishes to Speak","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.","desc":"Now that you can disguise yourself as a ruling member of the Twilight Council, I am certain Bor Wildmane will want to speak with you. Go see him, and prepare yourself for a very difficult mission...","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Yes, that's right, ‹name›. I have a very tough task ahead...","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79951":{"id":79951,"t":"Mummies a guide to the unsavory undead","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Mummies: A Guide to the Unsavory Undead","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nMummies: A Guide to the Unsavory Undead (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"911":{"id":911,"t":"Gateway to the Frontier","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take your ward to the Mor'shan Rampart in the northern part of the Barrens, just before entering Ashenvale.","desc":"They say that Ashenvale is the new frontier, and that the Mor'shan Rampart in the Barrens is the gateway to it. That would be so cool to be a pioneer, carving everything you need out of the untamed wilds! They say that this is where the Horde and Alliance will clash the most in the future, and I want to be there ‹name›!\nWould you take me to the Mor'shan Rampart so I can see what the frontier looks like, please? I wanna see where the Horde is driving out those smelly night elves!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Horde","back":"Are we there yet?","done":"Wow, Ashenvale is where real adventure happens! Have you ever fought in Ashenvale, ‹name›? When I become a hero when I grow up, I wanna come to Ashenvale and fight for the glory of the Horde!\nThank you for taking me to the frontier, ‹name›. You're the best!\nThe Barrens Open the zone on the world map Start Orcish Orphan End Orcish Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Horde Shareable No Quest ID 911\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 650 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Children's Week\nUse the Orcish Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nOrphan Matron Battlewail Orgrimmar\n2 [ 60 ] Gateway to the Frontier this quest\nTake your ward to the Mor'shan Rampart in the northern part of the Barrens, just before entering Ashenvale.\nOrcish Orphan\n650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1071":{"id":1071,"t":"A Gnome's Respite","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Venture Co. Loggers, and 10 Venture Co. Deforesters and return to Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon.\nVenture Co. Logger slain : 0/ 10\nVenture Co. Deforester slain : 0/ 10","desc":"You see, ‹name›, I'm a member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, and it's my goal... nay, my DUTY! to show the night elves that a blend of magic, mixtures, and mechanisms can help save their forests.\nBut it's a hard fought war, and the goblins reproduce like rabbits it seems. I haven't even had time to build my newest inventions!\nI need some time to plan and organize. But to do that, I need your help keeping the goblins at bay in Windshear Crag to the east...","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"How goes the battle on your end, ‹name›?","done":"Thanks so much for your help, ‹name›. You're actually back just in time.\nI think I've got the perfect plan. Explosives. No, that's not the plan, but it's part of the plan.\nSee, I've been using high explosives--don't worry, they're not as dangerous as everyone thinks--to scare the goblins back a bit. I can herd 'em pretty good with a few key detonations along the mountains' edges, but I've been low on supplies now for a few days.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"98191":{"id":98191,"t":"A friend of the family","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Menethil Statuette to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral of Light.\nProvided: Menethil Statuette","desc":"King Terenas was a good man. A devout man. Beloved by his people, and truly the reason we have this Alliance at all.\nThe irony is he was humble--he hated these sorts of memorials, and so precious few exist. And of those, few survived Lordaeron's fall.\nIt seems the Light has coalesced in this statuette. It would be best kept in the Cathedral of the Light in Cathdral Square, in the center of the city. Bring it to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker for safekeeping.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKnight's Lance Royal Dagger\nExperience: 200","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.2,"y":33,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"7791":{"id":7791,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by Stormwind for your generous actions. Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53.9,"y":81.7,"n":"Clavicus Knavingham","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"191":{"id":191,"t":"Panther Mastery","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Panthers.\nPanther slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Now you're ready to turn it up a notch. If you want to prove yourself worthy of socializing with the likes of these big game hunters, you'll need to prove that you can kill 10 panthers.\nThose big boys are tougher. They're not as easy as the young ones you were killing earlier.","rew":"Experience: 1,300","done":"Perfectly executed, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.5,"n":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"591":{"id":591,"t":"The Mind's Eye","lv":46,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Mind's Eye to Kin'weelay at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\nMind's Eye Mai'Zoth","desc":"The Mind's Eye is held by an ogre mage, east of here and deep within the Mosh'Ogg ogre mound. His name is Mai'Zoth. I know him from when the Darkspears dwelt in Stranglethorn - he is vicious, and his magic is strong.\nAnd if he has the Mind's Eye, then his magic will be stronger still.\nYou must face Mai'Zoth and wrest from him the Mind's Eye. It is a perilous task, but it is the only hope we have of saving Yenniku.","rew":"Experience: 5,050\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. The spirits sing praise of your bravery, yet they tell me no tales of your quest against Mai'Zoth.\nDo you have the Eye?","done":"You retrieved the eye! Your might is the stuff of legends, ‹name›!\nAnd in getting the Eye, you must have defeated Mai'Zoth and sent him to the Nether. That is why the spirits would not mention him before.\nIt is good that he is gone from the world of flesh and bone, but now that he is in the realm of spirits...I fear he will begin a new reign.\nBut that is a worry for another time. Now, I must perform a ritual to bend the Mind's Eye to our needs...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8991":{"id":8991,"t":"The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth Jarien and Sothos and slay them. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the recombined Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLord Valthalak's Amulet\nBrazier of Beckoning\nJarien slain\nSothos slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"The siblings, Jarien and Sothos, decided to join the Scarlet Crusade upon the disbanding of our mercenary company. They took the right piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet with them. Good riddance, I say, but we need that piece back.\nFrom what we could gather, they were actually slain by Grand Crusader Dathrohan himself for failing the initiation rites inside his chamber in the Scarlet Bastion.\nIn any case, we... meaning you, are still going to need to retrieve that piece of the amulet.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Does this mean then, ‹class›, that you've already put the souls of those two fools to rest and recombined the pieces of Lord Valthalak's amulet?","done":"I suppose it's for the best that the souls of those two have finally been put to rest, even if I didn't like them while they were alive. In any case, we have what we were after, and now the amulet is reassembled! But we still have the hardest test ahead of us.\nIn order for the brazier to be attuned to calling forth Lord Valthalak, there are a few more items that need to be gathered and brought back to me here.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"351":{"id":351,"t":"Find OOX-17/TN!","lv":48,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the distress beacon to Oglethorpe's homing robot.\nOOX-17/TN Distress Beacon Murderous Blisterpaw 1 % , Gor'marok the Ravager 1 % , Zerillis 1 % in Zul'Farrak , Dustwraith 1 % in Zul'Farrak and 4 more\nProvided: OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon","desc":"You have uncovered some sort of strange, egg-shaped device made from metal. Fiddling with one of its knobs springs the egg to life, as it opens up into some sort of gnomish robotic contraption! A voice from inside the robotic egg crackles to life.\n\"The name's Oglethorpe, and my homing robot has gone missing! I will reward you for its recovery! Please take this beacon to the robot. Excellent, I now have computed the coordinates for you! It crashed near the Gaping Chasm in Tanaris!\"","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"You appear to have uncovered the wreckage of... a robotic chicken? The voice from within the egg crackles to life again:\n\"Yes, excellent work! This is indeed my homing robot, though my sensors indicate that it needs a jump start before it can fly back to Booty Bay for repairs. Go ahead and place the beacon inside the rover. The beacon will take care of the rest!\"","done":"You place the egg... distress beacon... inside the chicken... homing robot.\nHums and whirs are heard from inside the robot as it struggles to stand up. After the robot comes to life, Oglethorpe's voice is heard once more, but now from inside the robot:\n\"OOX-17/TN is working at least, but it needs major repairs! It is much too heavy for you to carry it... but I think I have an idea. Are you up for watching over it some more?\"","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":60.2,"y":64.7,"n":"Homing Robot OOX-17/TN","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8751":{"id":8751,"t":"The Protector of Kalimdor","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 9,950\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Never have I seen such tenacity! The Bronze Flight grants you one final enchantment. The Timeless One himself has requested it so!\nHand me your signet ring so that I may make the necessary adjustments.","done":"Rise, Protector of Kalimdor! Rise and be recognized!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"5151":{"id":5151,"t":"Hypercapacitor Gizmo","lv":30,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay the beast and bring back the Hypercapacitor Gizmo and Panther Cage Key to Wizlo Bearingshiner.\nPanther Cage Key\nHypercapacitor Gizmo Enraged Panther\nProvided: Panther Cage Key","desc":"I am the only survivor from our caravan attack by the centaur! A rare yet mighty panther is guarding my best gizmo, which is around his neck. Hah! Even the centaur tremble in the presence of this ferocious beast!\nHere is the key to the cage. They took everything there, but left him alone. Slay this beast and bring back my hypercapacitor, and I shall reward you.\nThe wrecked caravan is just north of here.","rew":"You will receive:\nInventor's League Ring\nExperience: 3,050","back":"Do you have my hypercapacitor?","done":"My hypercapacitor! This will keep me busy for a while until I can figure out what it does...","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":21.4,"y":32.6,"n":"Wizlo Bearingshiner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1151":{"id":1151,"t":"Test of Strength","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Fragments of Rok'Alim to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.\nFragments of Rok'Alim Rok'Alim the Pounder","desc":"During the time of the Old Gods, elementals inhabited much of this world. They worshipped the Old Gods, and the Gods, through their power, kept the elementals bound to this world. When the Old Gods were banished, the elementals faded from our world and now only return at the bidding of powerful mages.\nThere are exceptions though. Some elementals were powerful enough to remain here on their own. One such elemental is Rok'Alim.\nTo test your strength, find Rok'Alim in Thousand Needles and slay him.","rew":"Experience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Rok'Alim is also called the Pounder by the centaur tribes in Thousand Needles because of the thundering his fists make as he pummels the creatures brave, or stupid, enough to stand in his path.","done":"The Test of Strength is done. You have shown strength and bravery, and you are now prepared for the final test before these rites are completed.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":53.9,"y":41.5,"n":"Dorn Plainstalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"431":{"id":431,"t":"Candles of Beckoning","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCandle of Beckoning","done":"You grab one of the candles and place it in your pack.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":68.2,"y":42,"n":"Crate of Candles","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"1471":{"id":1471,"t":"The Binding","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Runes of Summoning, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Runes of Summoning to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\nSummoned Voidwalker slain\nProvided: Runes of Summoning","desc":"Surely you have seen the circle of summoning below us? Only there will you be able to draw forth an unbound voidwalker.\nUsing these runes, you will be able to draw it forth, and then you must dominate it through strength of arms and magic.\nWhen it is subdued, it will be indentured to you. Come to me then, and I will elucidate the spell of summoning, so that it may serve you to whatever end you wish.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Voidwalker\nExperience: 625","back":"I expect to hear of your success, ‹name›. Not meeting my expectations will be the least of your worries, however, should you fail.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. Now, I will impart to you the spell used for summoning the voidwalker.\nThe power that it unleashed upon you is now yours to command. Use it wisely.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":26,"n":"Carendin Halgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"3631":{"id":3631,"t":"Summon Felsteed","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Strahad Farsan in the Barrens.","desc":"Hmph. I say you're not prepared, but that is not my decision. Strahad feels otherwise, and it is his decision to make... this time.\nHe wishes to speak to you, and quickly. You'll find him still above Ratchet in the Barrens, at his little tower there with his acolytes.\nDo not dawdle long.","done":"Good luck, ‹name›. I look forward to seeing you in the future.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Zevrost","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7631":{"id":7631,"t":"Dreadsteed of Xoroth","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Read Mor'zul's Instructions. Summon a Xorothian Dreadsteed, defeat it, then bind its spirit to you.\nXorothian Dreadsteed slain\nProvided: Mor'zul's Instructions","desc":"All the preparations are made. Now, you must perform the ritual to create a Circle of Greater Summoning, then use the parchment infused with Xorothian stardust... to open a portal to Xoroth.\nI have written the instructions for the ritual onto a scroll. Study it closely, for you must perform each step exactly if you wish to succeed.\nFortune to you, ‹name›. And may the souls of your enemies swiftly find their way into your shard pouch.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Dreadsteed\nExperience: 6,600","done":"The Xorothian Dreadsteed's spirit is beaten. Although rage pulses through its ghostly flanks, you know that the beast's soul is yours...\nIt whispers dark magic into your mind and instills within you the knowledge to summon a dreadsteed.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.7,"y":31.6,"n":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1711":{"id":1711,"t":"Mathiel's Armor","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Hardened Leggings\nExperience: 3,050","done":"I have finished with your piece of armor, and I am quite pleased. Furen's new techniques meshed perfectly with my own and I am sure this armor will prove to be quite resilient.\nThank you, ‹name›. And may this serve you well in future battles.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":59.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Mathiel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1791":{"id":1791,"t":"The Windwatcher","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Bath'rah the Windwatcher.","desc":"Now that you've learned your berserker's stance, you'll want a nice weapon to use it with.\nTalk to Bath'rah the Windwatcher, a troll hermit who lives between the Alterac Mountains and the Western Plaguelands. He is a skilled weapon maker and a powerful shaman.\nTo find Bath'rah, go to the river that flows along Tarren Mill's eastern flank. Follow it north--Bath'rah is camped near ruins that rest along the river's eastern bank.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"You have traveled far, young warrior. I see fire in your eyes. You seek a weapon of great power, yes?\nI can help you with your quest. And you can help me with mine.\nThe Barrens Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":68.6,"y":49.2,"n":"Klannoc Macleod","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8431":{"id":8431,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"7871":{"id":7871,"t":"Vanquish the Invaders!","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,750 experience instead of 3,300, 0.83 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Horde, obtain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and return to Sentinel Farsong at the Silverwing Grove.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Beyond this tunnel you will find a field of strife and turmoil, young ‹class›. The Horde continue to decimate our sacred forest, cutting down the evergreen foliage to power their machines of war.\nEnter Warsong Gulch and defend Silverwing Hold. Push back the invading Horde forces!\nDo this, and earn a talisman of merit. Bring me such a talisman, ‹name›, and I shall reward you.","rew":"Money: 1 10 1 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Human, Dwarf, Night Elf, Gnome Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7871","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5231":{"id":5231,"t":"Target: Dalson's Tears","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Dalson's Tears in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nDalson's Tears Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Malvinious\nEmpty Dalson's Tears Bottle\nProvided: Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle","desc":"One of the plague cauldrons is located in the field of a former farmhouse now referred to as Dalson's Tears. No tears will be shed this day, ‹class›; we must strike at this cauldron and gain access to it!\nGo to Dalson's Tears, almost due north of Andorhal, and eliminate the cauldron lord there. It should have a key like the last one did, allowing you inside the cauldron's innards. Use this bottle to obtain a sample from inside the cauldron; each cauldron has its own distinct brew of toxins it uses.","rew":"Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"The skeletal key found on the cauldron lord easily slides into a keyhole and then disappears, allowing you permanent access to it. Crude, viscous ichors pulsate through twisted tubes within the cauldrons underpinnings.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":46.2,"y":51.9,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92911":{"id":92911,"t":"Harvesting the harvesters","lv":15,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm wants you to bring him 8 Golem Isosprings, 4 Copper Modulators, and a Crude Scope.\n8 Golem Isospring\n4 Copper Modulator\nCrude Scope","desc":"I see... this gives me some insight into what makes those monsters tick. I have an idea how we could override their systems, at least momentarily.\nI'll continue tinkering with the assembly you brought me. In the meantime, could you scrounge up some parts for the device?","rew":"You will receive:\nHarvester Override Signalcaster Schematic: Harvester Override Signalcaster\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 800\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"How's the project coming, Raton?","done":"Here it is, Raton! Should work great. Go give it a try!\n...Me? No, I'll stay here. It's starting to feel like home, anyway.\nWestfall The Barrens Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":51.6,"y":32.2,"n":"Ozwin Ironsprocket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92751":{"id":92751,"t":"Detonation at a distance","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Remote Detonator Kit to Sprite Jumpsprocket in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.\nProvided: Remote Detonator Kit","desc":"You need something destroyed? Would this have anything to do with your activities in Moonbrook? Don't look surprised. SI:7 stays apprised of all that goes on in Stormwind's lands.\nIf you're planning to set off an explosion in the caves below Westfall, you'll want to be well outside beforehand. Take this remote detonator - it's a recent prototype from our own engineers.\nOh - and it would be best if you didn't mention my involvement to your elf friend.","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Great - that's the detonator we need!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.2,"y":58.8,"n":"Jasper Fel","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":54.6,"y":8,"n":"Sprite Jumpsprocket","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"93951":{"id":93951,"t":"A little beauty","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Hippogryph Down feathers in the Shen'dar Highlands.\n8 Hippogryph Down","desc":"The Hippogryph that have taken up residence southwest of the village can be a nuisance, but they also present a rather unique opportunity to obtain their feathers. Many skyborne love to adorn their hair with vibrant plumes and the down feathers of a hippogryph are exceptionally vibrant and more importantly, silky soft.\nIf you are heading that way, try and gather as many of the fallen feathers as you can from in and around their nesting grounds. Do be careful, as wild hippogryph are not tolerant of guests.","rew":"Money: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 480\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"What beautiful things did you bring me?","done":"It might seem a bit of a vain triviality, gathering feathers for our hair. However, even in times like these, one needs to embrace the small joys as much as possible.\nIf one thing I create brings someone joy, then I will consider that to be a good day. Thank you for bringing me these and helping me bring some joy to Zephras.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Taleen Shimmerthread","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"2991":{"id":2991,"t":"Nekrum's Medallion","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Nekrum's Medallion to Thadius Grimshade in the Blasted Lands.\nNekrum's Medallion Nekrum Gutchewer","desc":"I'll find out where your gryphon is, but first you have to do something for me. There's a troll in Zul'Farrak, Nekrum Gutchewer, who possesses a medallion I would very much like to study. Bring me that Medallion and I'll use my powers to find Sharpbeak.\nZul'Farrak is across the ocean to the west, in the desert of Tanaris.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,250\n+150 reputation with Wildhammer Clan\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have Nekrum's Medallion, ‹name›? There are powers hidden within it that I am eager to discover.","done":"Ah, the medallion of Nekrum. It is rumored to have given the troll an unnatural long life, but at a cost. I hope to discover a way to reap the medallion's power while avoiding its... unpleasant side effects.\nYou have done me a service, ‹name›. I shall now uphold my end of our bargain.\nBlasted Lands Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":66.9,"y":19.5,"n":"Thadius Grimshade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]},"8111":{"id":8111,"t":"Enchanted South Seas Kelp","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Enchanted South Seas Kelp","rew":"You will receive:\nEnchanted South Seas Kelp\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Hey mon! It be good to see you again. The tribe be talking about your killin' of the Hakkari and all that. Molthor gave me the word to be adding more mojo to your talisman. Just give it here and Maywiki make it better.","done":"The neck piece not be for smokin', mon! You got to use it to fight evil.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]},"8191":{"id":8191,"t":"Prophetic Aura","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Hakkari Witch Doctor 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Gurubashi Blood Drinker 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Cub 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Voodoo Slave 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nProphetic Aura\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8191","cats":["zulgurub"]}});